			 (dub.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				295
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δοκοῦντα,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μηδὲν ὄντα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				613
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ᾽ ἀρετῆς δοκούσης ἐς ἀλλήλους
					γίγνεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.10
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be an established, current opinion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				76b24
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δοκοῦντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1088a16
				</span></i>
			, al.:— 
